  "detail": "Same frame, and no conflict is constructible from the evidence we hold. Across 28 committed traces, 9 carry a whole-series RSD >= 30% and NOT ONE of them publishes a tail figure -- every one returns NO_STEADY_TAIL, or a MARGINAL_TAIL that withholds its median. Conversely the largest whole-series RSD among the 12 publishing traces is 10.36%, against a smallest of 34.39% among the large-spread set: the two sets are disjoint and well separated. Switch's 70% spread and Niobe's steady tail have never described the same published number, and cannot -- a large spread is exactly the condition under which the tail refuses. Both instruments are correct over their own selection and neither needs repair on this account."
